OSP Prometheus Metrics
Open Service Platform

!!! Introduction

The <*poco.prometheus*> bundle exports metrics of the OSP process in the
Prometheus text format: the process metrics, the threads of the default thread
pool and of the web server thread pool, the connections of the web servers,
the requests that the web server dispatcher has handled and the number of active
web sessions. The metrics of the web servers have the label "server", whose
value is protocol://host:port. The metrics of the thread pools have the label
"name", whose value is the name of the thread pool ("default" for the default
thread pool).

The bundle serves the metrics with its own HTTP server, and can also write
them to the log at a fixed interval.

NOTE: The metrics server listens on all interfaces by default, without TLS,
and without authentication unless prometheus.permission is set. The
metrics show the load of the process and of its web servers. Set
prometheus.host to 127.0.0.1 if only local clients may read them.
With prometheus.permission, the user names and passwords of the OSP users
are sent in clear text (HTTP Basic authentication), unless a proxy in front
of the metrics server terminates TLS.


!!! Configuring the Prometheus Bundle

The bundle is configured using the global application configuration file.
The following configuration properties are available:


!! prometheus.enable

Set to true to collect and export the metrics. Default is false.


!! prometheus.host

The address the metrics server listens on. Default is 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces).


!! prometheus.port

The port of the metrics server. Default is 9100. With 0, the metrics server
is not started.


!! prometheus.path

The path of the metrics. Default is /metrics. Requests for other paths are
answered with 404 Not Found.


!! prometheus.permission

The permission a user needs to read the metrics. If set, a request must carry
HTTP Basic credentials, which the auth service checks (see
osp.web.authServiceName). The answer is 401 Unauthorized without valid
credentials, 403 Forbidden for a user without the permission, and
503 Service Unavailable while the auth service is not available. Default is
empty: every client can read the metrics.


!! osp.web.authServiceName

The name of the auth service that checks the credentials. Default is "osp.auth".


!! prometheus.server.maxQueued

The maximum number of queued connections of the metrics server. Default is 8.


!! prometheus.server.maxThreads

The maximum number of threads of the metrics server. Default is 2.


!! prometheus.server.keepAlive

Set to true to keep the connections of the metrics server open for further
requests. Default is false.


!! prometheus.server.keepAliveTime

The time in seconds after which an idle connection is closed. Default is 10.


!! prometheus.server.maxKeepAlive

The maximum number of requests on one connection. Default is 10.


!! prometheus.log.enable

Set to true to write the metrics to the logger "Metrics" at information level.
Default is false.


!! prometheus.log.interval

The interval in seconds at which the metrics are written to the log, between
1 and 2147483 (almost 25 days). Default is 30. With prometheus.enable and
prometheus.log.enable set to true and a value outside this range, the bundle
does not start.
